// Martin's ISP example (Agile Software Development, chapter 12), the violating version: one UI interface holds
// the dialogue of every transaction. Four axes: the three transactions, each changing for its own banking reason,
// and the user interface, which changes with the device. The interface's methods belong to the transactions they
// serve: each is foreign to UI, a container of the ui axis (the fat interface, Clause 3), and each transaction
// uses the ui axis, which changes more often than it (the uses, Clause 1).
axis transaction = [martin.isp.transaction]
axis deposit     = [martin.isp.deposit, martin.isp.ui.UI.requestDepositAmount()]
axis withdrawal  = [martin.isp.withdrawal, martin.isp.ui.UI.requestWithdrawalAmount()]
axis transfer    = [martin.isp.transfer, martin.isp.ui.UI.requestTransferAmount()]
axis ui          = [martin.isp.ui]
// the speed order: the transactions change for banking reasons, the user interface with the device
speed transaction < deposit, withdrawal, transfer < ui;
